# The concurrency rule (IR-13, AT.33): the house's append-only logs merge line-wise, so two sessions'
# appends never conflict; house/guards.py and tools/catalog.py refuse a duplicate id that a union merge
# lets through (AP-review-0002, A1). house/guards.json declares the logs; this block mirrors it.
# house guards: union logs (IR-13): begin
house/branches.jsonl merge=union
house/atlas-replies.jsonl merge=union
catalog/events.jsonl merge=union
# house guards: union logs (IR-13): end

# Git LFS for binaries only, and LF line endings for text (AP-all-0006, the atlas's set, AT.2).
# Text never goes to LFS, so it diffs, merges and audits line by line; SVG is text on purpose.
# A binary that can be regenerated is not committed at all. Patterns the house already had stay as they were.
# lfs: binaries only (AP-all-0006): begin
*.png   filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.jpg   filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.jpeg  filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.gif   filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
